WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.059
(crowd applauds)
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:01.059 --> 00:00:03.611
You're like a dying breed,
the natural redhead.

00:00:03.611 --> 00:00:05.149
It's so beautiful.

00:00:05.149 --> 00:00:05.982
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:05.982 --> 00:00:07.998
- I'm, like, jealous, I can't
ever keep red in my hair,

00:00:07.998 --> 00:00:10.606
it won't stick, I tried so hard years ago.

00:00:10.606 --> 00:00:11.749
- It really just falls out?

00:00:11.749 --> 00:00:12.765
Like, as soon as you get in
the shower, its like, gone?

00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:14.735
- Like, literally my hair rejects red.

00:00:14.735 --> 00:00:15.844
I don't know.

00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:18.045
Which is funny because my mom
has red in her hair naturally.

00:00:18.045 --> 00:00:19.026
I don't get it either.

00:00:19.026 --> 00:00:19.859
We don't need to know this.

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:21.757
(audience laughs)

00:00:21.757 --> 00:00:22.902
Say hello to Mario.

00:00:22.902 --> 00:00:23.735
- How are you?

00:00:23.735 --> 00:00:24.623
- Hi Mario, how are you?

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:25.762
- I'm well, thank you.

00:00:25.762 --> 00:00:27.002
I'm excited to see Willow.

00:00:27.002 --> 00:00:29.032
I was just telling Kelly I
was a fan back in the day,

00:00:29.032 --> 00:00:29.865
of the original.

00:00:29.865 --> 00:00:31.421
- Yeah, we were around
when the original was...

00:00:31.421 --> 00:00:32.790
(audience applauds)

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.145
- That must have been like 35
years ago or something, right?

00:00:35.145 --> 00:00:36.385
- Yeah, it was '88, yeah.

00:00:36.385 --> 00:00:37.652
- Yeah, woo.

00:00:37.652 --> 00:00:38.676
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:38.676 --> 00:00:40.831
- My math's not that good,
but it's, like, 30 something.

00:00:40.831 --> 00:00:42.351
- Yeah, it's years.

00:00:42.351 --> 00:00:43.791
Watch out though, he knows jiu-jitsu, so.

00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:44.624
- I know.

00:00:44.624 --> 00:00:45.457
Watch out, that'll save you.

00:00:45.457 --> 00:00:46.380
- She could choke you.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.712
- Did you play sports or do
anything like that growing up?

00:00:48.712 --> 00:00:49.614
- I did actually.

00:00:49.614 --> 00:00:52.451
I played a little bit of netball
and a little bit of hockey.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:53.284
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:00:53.284 --> 00:00:54.117
- So yeah.

00:00:54.117 --> 00:00:54.950
- [Kelly] Hockey?

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.783
- Yes.

00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:56.616
- That's fun.

00:00:56.616 --> 00:00:57.449
- It was really fun.

00:00:57.449 --> 00:00:58.680
- Did you slam people
into the walls and stuff?

00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.800
- I mean, it was pretty aggressive.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.072
We were on AstroTurf and we
did knock about quite a bit,

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:03.905
and, you know-

00:01:03.905 --> 00:01:04.738
- Knock about.

00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:05.571
I love your accent.

00:01:05.571 --> 00:01:06.695
Okay.
(crowd laughs)

00:01:06.695 --> 00:01:07.528
- Great expression.

00:01:07.528 --> 00:01:10.667
- So did you know you
wanted to act early on?

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.854
- Yeah, I mean I always
just loved it at school.

00:01:12.854 --> 00:01:15.094
I had this, like, really
passionate drama teacher

00:01:15.094 --> 00:01:17.507
who used to put on
plays at local theaters.

00:01:17.507 --> 00:01:19.307
And he was very serious about it,

00:01:19.307 --> 00:01:22.136
like, members of the public
would come in and watch it

00:01:22.136 --> 00:01:23.934
and it was quite an intense thing, yeah.

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:25.464
- That's cool that he's
serious about it though,

00:01:25.464 --> 00:01:26.686
that made you more passionate about it.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.686
- Yeah, definitely.

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:30.856
I mean, I was so passionate
that I remember one time

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:32.904
my parents would send me to Stagecoach,

00:01:32.904 --> 00:01:34.463
like, after school and stuff,

00:01:34.463 --> 00:01:36.263
and I'd fallen off a trampoline

00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:38.136
and I went to Stagecoach,
because I was convinced

00:01:38.136 --> 00:01:39.936
that I had to go even though
I wasn't feeling great,

00:01:39.936 --> 00:01:41.664
and my elbow hurt a little bit.

00:01:41.664 --> 00:01:44.336
And then at the end of
the day it turned out

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.944
that I had to go to A&amp;E
because I had basically

00:01:46.944 --> 00:01:51.472
broken my elbow, and I had
been, like, dancing all day...

00:01:51.472 --> 00:01:53.559
- Adrenaline, it's beautiful thing.

00:01:53.559 --> 00:01:54.512
(audience laughs)
- Yeah, it is.

00:01:54.512 --> 00:01:56.310
- It'll get you through some situations.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.897
You're like, "I guess we
are powerful, humans."

00:01:58.897 --> 00:01:59.730
That stinks.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.647
But that sounds like fun though

00:02:00.647 --> 00:02:02.316
to get to do at such a young age as well.

00:02:02.316 --> 00:02:03.149
- Yeah, I loved it.

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:04.276
I was, like, really determined.

00:02:04.276 --> 00:02:05.203
- Awesome, awesome.

00:02:05.203 --> 00:02:08.164
Well, you're from the UK,
obviously, with your accent,

00:02:08.164 --> 00:02:11.002
but you had to do a Texas
accent for one role.

00:02:11.002 --> 00:02:11.835
- Yes.

00:02:11.835 --> 00:02:15.196
- I'm curious how you mastered
that, it's very redneck.

00:02:15.196 --> 00:02:17.545
(audience laughs)

00:02:17.545 --> 00:02:19.236
- I loved getting to master it,

00:02:19.236 --> 00:02:21.327
well, I mean, have a go at mastering that.

00:02:21.327 --> 00:02:23.127
I watched so much Friday Night Lights.

00:02:23.127 --> 00:02:25.704
Like, I think I watched
every single episode

00:02:25.704 --> 00:02:27.127
over and over again.

00:02:27.127 --> 00:02:29.154
- That series is actually based on a town

00:02:29.154 --> 00:02:30.225
that's literally next to mine.

00:02:30.225 --> 00:02:31.058
- No way.

00:02:31.058 --> 00:02:31.891
- [Mario] Tyler, right?

00:02:31.891 --> 00:02:32.724
- I'm telling you,

00:02:32.724 --> 00:02:35.802
it's literally like every
small town in Texas.

00:02:35.802 --> 00:02:37.951
That was a really good thing
to base your accent on.

00:02:37.951 --> 00:02:38.984
(Ellie laughs)

00:02:38.984 --> 00:02:39.817
- I loved it.

00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:41.219
Like, I was totally obsessed.

00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:42.128
Connie Britton was just, yeah.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.918
- Oh my gosh, such a great...

00:02:43.918 --> 00:02:45.870
Well, and he's not bad to look at.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.008
- No, he's not bad.

00:02:47.008 --> 00:02:48.518
- Yeah, he is very cute.

00:02:48.518 --> 00:02:50.422
You've spent some time
in Texas as well, right?

00:02:50.422 --> 00:02:51.255
Do you like Texas?

00:02:51.255 --> 00:02:52.302
- Oh yeah, I a sister
that lives in Houston.

00:02:52.302 --> 00:02:53.270
- [Kelly] Oh, right on.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.103
- A lot of time in Texas.

00:02:54.103 --> 00:02:54.936
- The food is pretty good.

00:02:54.936 --> 00:02:55.769
Do you have an accent?

00:02:55.769 --> 00:02:56.620
Do you have a Texas accent?

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.340
- I, like, adopt any accent I'm visiting

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.049
so I'll drop a lot of y'all's
after I leave outta Texas.

00:03:01.049 --> 00:03:03.489
After I'm in New York,
I'll be talking like this.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:05.980
You know, I'll just,
like, adopt whatever I...

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:06.813
- You adapt wherever you are?

00:03:06.813 --> 00:03:07.646
- Yeah, exactly.

00:03:07.646 --> 00:03:08.479
- [Kelly] Blend in.

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:09.312
- Yeah, I try.

00:03:09.312 --> 00:03:11.977
- Well, okay, so you're
now in the Disney+ show,

00:03:11.977 --> 00:03:12.940
it's a series, Willow,

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.148
which we know from when we were younger.

00:03:14.148 --> 00:03:15.529
But tell us about the show, is it similar?

00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:18.068
Is it kind of based
off of that, obviously?

00:03:18.068 --> 00:03:20.607
- Yeah, so it's a kind
of a sequel to the film,

00:03:20.607 --> 00:03:23.557
it takes place like 20 years
after the original film.

00:03:23.557 --> 00:03:26.357
And it's about this
group of unlikely heroes

00:03:26.357 --> 00:03:28.868
that go on a quest with Willow

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:32.439
to find our damsel in distress,
who is actually a prince.

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:35.647
So we go off on this
adventure and start, kind of,

00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:39.068
discovering quite interesting
things about ourselves.

00:03:39.068 --> 00:03:40.959
- There's quite a lot
of wit in it as well,

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:42.108
like, it's very funny.

00:03:42.108 --> 00:03:44.218
- Yeah, it's quite a funny show, yeah.

00:03:44.218 --> 00:03:46.258
I mean, we had a lot of fun making it.

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:48.698
We were in Wales and it
was really wonderful.

00:03:48.698 --> 00:03:49.531
- It's pretty to look at,

00:03:49.531 --> 00:03:50.364
scene photography was nice, yeah.

00:03:50.364 --> 00:03:52.019
- [Kelly] Wales is pretty, yeah.

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:53.897
I love touring over
there, Wales is so pretty.

00:03:53.897 --> 00:03:54.730
- So beautiful.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:58.035
Like, the Brecon Beacons are just like...

00:03:58.035 --> 00:04:00.584
Oh, it's so gorgeous, the
forests and everything,

00:04:00.584 --> 00:04:01.417
so untouched.

00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:03.095
- Just a fun show to do,
like, a fantasy type vibe,

00:04:03.095 --> 00:04:03.936
that must be kind of fun,

00:04:03.936 --> 00:04:06.384
because you're, like, talking
about magic, I love that.

00:04:06.384 --> 00:04:07.706
- I do, I get to do a lot of magic.

00:04:07.706 --> 00:04:09.424
- That's like, right up my alley.

00:04:09.424 --> 00:04:11.296
So you must have had to
keep your character's

00:04:11.296 --> 00:04:12.896
identity a secret for a while.

00:04:12.896 --> 00:04:13.813
Is it hard?

00:04:14.725 --> 00:04:16.805
Don't tell me anything if
you wanted to be a secret,

00:04:16.805 --> 00:04:18.354
I'm not a good secret keeper.

00:04:18.354 --> 00:04:21.197
Like, are you good at that?

00:04:21.197 --> 00:04:23.203
- I definitely found it difficult,

00:04:23.203 --> 00:04:25.096
and I also definitely found it difficult

00:04:25.096 --> 00:04:28.205
when my castmates would play pranks on me.

00:04:28.205 --> 00:04:31.746
So I actually had this
one time I received a text

00:04:31.746 --> 00:04:34.596
from an unknown number, basically saying,

00:04:34.596 --> 00:04:37.136
"I am from a tabloid
newspaper and I have-"

00:04:37.136 --> 00:04:37.969
- That's wrong.

00:04:37.969 --> 00:04:40.245
- "I have found out who your character is,

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:43.756
please can you send an image
to go with the article?"

00:04:43.756 --> 00:04:44.917
And I freaked out.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.077
I mean, I called everyone, like,

00:04:46.077 --> 00:04:47.647
the whole of my team, everyone.

00:04:47.647 --> 00:04:49.658
- And they're all laughing, no.

00:04:49.658 --> 00:04:51.272
- No, they were all freaking out.

00:04:51.272 --> 00:04:52.105
- [Kelly] Oh, I thought
they knew and were in on it.

00:04:52.105 --> 00:04:53.572
- And Disney were freaking out,

00:04:53.572 --> 00:04:55.322
like, someone spilled
coffee down themselves,

00:04:55.322 --> 00:04:57.749
it was, like, a whole situation.

00:04:57.749 --> 00:04:59.189
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:59.189 --> 00:05:02.610
- And then I found out that it was Dempsey

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:03.998
who was in the show with
me, he had just been like-

00:05:03.998 --> 00:05:05.459
- Oh, Dempsey.

00:05:05.459 --> 00:05:06.292
- Dempsey, I mean-

00:05:06.292 --> 00:05:07.125
- Dempsey's wilding out.

00:05:07.125 --> 00:05:08.377
- Dempsey is so wild.

00:05:08.377 --> 00:05:10.659
And he would just pull these
pranks again and again.

00:05:10.659 --> 00:05:12.218
So every time he says something, I'm like-

00:05:12.218 --> 00:05:14.140
- It sounded real, even
how he played it out.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:16.227
- Yeah, totally.

00:05:16.227 --> 00:05:17.396
But he just got...

00:05:17.396 --> 00:05:19.284
I think he started to get
more and more extreme,

00:05:19.284 --> 00:05:20.874
like, he said, like,
"Oh, I heard that you had

00:05:20.874 --> 00:05:22.926
a really severe accident
at the read through."

00:05:22.926 --> 00:05:24.826
And then I kind of was
like, hmm, I'm onto you now.

00:05:24.826 --> 00:05:25.659
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:25.659 --> 00:05:26.492
- Yeah.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.325
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:27.325 --> 00:05:28.547
I love people that play pranks,

00:05:28.547 --> 00:05:30.357
it keeps this set kind of fun as well.

00:05:30.357 --> 00:05:31.190
- [Ellie] Definitely.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.539
- Not for the guy who got coffee on him.

00:05:32.539 --> 00:05:34.138
(Ellie and audience laugh)

00:05:34.138 --> 00:05:36.568
But is it true that Ron
told you to take the magic

00:05:36.568 --> 00:05:38.058
very seriously?

00:05:38.058 --> 00:05:41.339
- Yeah, I got on a Zoom
with the whole team

00:05:41.339 --> 00:05:44.259
and Ron told me that I really
needed to do some research

00:05:44.259 --> 00:05:46.467
into magic and take it seriously.

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:49.448
And so I ended up, like,
running about London

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.308
to every, kind of, magic
shop that I could find,

00:05:52.308 --> 00:05:55.627
and I kind of intensely studied magic

00:05:55.627 --> 00:05:57.808
only to realize that the magic in our show

00:05:57.808 --> 00:05:59.828
was totally different to anything

00:05:59.828 --> 00:06:01.858
that I had actually discovered.

00:06:01.858 --> 00:06:03.109
- But your card trick
game is on point now.

00:06:03.109 --> 00:06:04.479
- Yeah, insane, yeah.
(crowd laughs)

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:05.312
- [Kelly] "But I can pull
a rabbit out of a hat."

00:06:05.312 --> 00:06:07.300
- "Pick a card, any card."

